-// (see /vagrant/oem-reference/protocol-reverse/inventory.json).
+// What the BIOS reads before deciding what to push, and the single most
+// dangerous route we serve.
+//
+// THE BUG THAT COST THREE HOST CRASHES: every earlier attempt modelled this
+// response on /vagrant/oem-reference/protocol-reverse/inventory.json -- but
+// that file is the BIOS's POST *payload*, not the BMC's GET *response*.  We
+// were replying with the shape of the request.  The BIOS's RfInventory driver
+// walked a document with none of the fields it expected and #GP'd at a
+// constant RIP.
